title: On the beat
intro: Spawners, turrets, moving platforms and switches can step to the music's beat instead of counting seconds.
project: Platformer | Beat Steps

chapter: A clock to step to | Beat Clock
say: The Platformer template plays a theme tune. A Beat Clock on the music keeps time with it.
select: Music
add: BeatClock
expectcomponents: Music = Transform, BackgroundMusic, BeatClock

chapter: A lift that steps | Mover Beats
select: Lift
explain: component:Mover | Mover | The lift is a Mover. It goes up and down at its speed, waiting a second at each end.
set: Mover.Beats = 4
set: Mover.Speed = 12
explain: field:Mover.Beats | Beats | With Beats set, it steps instead: it sets off on every fourth beat, once a bar, gets to its next point, and waits there for the next step.
expectvalue: Lift.Mover.Beats = 4
explain: field:Mover.BeatOffset | Beat Offset and Clock | Beat Offset steps it later by that many beats, so two lifts on every other beat can take turns. Clock picks which clock to follow; empty is the scene's first.

chapter: A bridge on the beat | Switch Beats
select: Lever
explain: component:Switch | Switch | The lever brings out the bridge while it's on.
set: Switch.Beats = 2
explain: field:Switch.Beats | Beats | Now it also flips itself every two beats, so the bridge comes and goes with the music.
expectvalue: Lever.Switch.Beats = 2

chapter: Sparkles on the beat | Spawner Beats
create: Empty
rename: Sparkler
set: Transform.Position.X = -3
set: Transform.Position.Y = 4
add: Spawner
pick: Spawner.Prefab = Sparkle
set: Spawner.Beats = 1
set: Spawner.MaxAlive = 4
explain: field:Spawner.Beats | Beats | A spawner with Beats spawns on every beat rather than every interval. A shooter works the same way, firing on the beat.
expectvalue: Sparkler.Spawner.Beats = 1
say: Let's hear it. Watch the lift set off once a bar, the bridge come and go every two beats, and a sparkle on every beat.
look: -8, 0, 7
play
wait: 8
stop
say: Rhythm platformers and bullet patterns that pulse with the soundtrack, with no code.
